{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917480012},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a data question that I need to answer using the xorq verifier framework. The user is asking for farmers markets per 100,000 residents, which is a metric combining two datasets:\n\n1. Farmers markets by state: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\n2. Census data (population): https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\n\nFollowing the protocol, I should:\n1. Check for semantic models first with xorq_semantic_models\n2. Check existing aliases with xorq_catalog_list_aliases\n3. Only if no existing alias covers this, ingest the sources and create the metric\n4. Use xorq_select to compute the value\n5. Use xorq_verify to verify the result\n\nLet me start by exploring what's in the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you answer this question following the verified data workflow. Let me start by checking what's available in the xorq catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_013evmGEj7XRTKsoz1eVpn4Y","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01DyuPbdv9n2rkwix7q2TdMu","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":380,"cach